    "notes": "Campaign spatial prototype, not canonical geography. City 2.3 km across; walls 55 m, city hill 380 m, central acropolis 490 m. Spire 1.8 km high, 7.16 km WSW: its tapered shadow reaches the city near 17:12 at true scale. Crater ~30 km across, floor -180 m, night flood +80 m. Tree ~31.5 km west of city, height 420 m. Hollow Mountains 4\u20137 km relief to north. Six 90 m statues scattered 12.5\u201314.9 km from city. Day crossing over broken ground ~16+ hours at assumed 2 km/h, before detours. Sea slider is a manual flood preview, independent of sun. No multiplayer or campaign clock yet. Erosion disabled deliberately for rapid spatial iteration and preservation of city platforms; may be enabled experimentally.",
